# cyrus-sasl, toolchain llvm
PKG_CFLAGS+=" -Wno-deprecated-non-prototype -Wno-sign-compare"
### saslauthd/md5.c clears its buffers through the address of the array (unsigned char (*)[65] where
### the prototype asks for unsigned char *): the same address, and gcc only warns. clang makes an
### incompatible pointer an error, which the warning it stays under gcc is enough of
PKG_CFLAGS+=" -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types"
